2026-11-26T05:25:36 | Claude chunk C | done | Chunk C done, branch agent/editor tip 8de5302 (one commit, TaskManager/wwwroot/css/app.css only).\nCause: .hov:hover/.hov:focus-visible set color: var(--on-fill) (dark text meant for a pastel --fill). The title input (and the note title) carry .hov but their background is transparent, so on focus/hover the text turned #181c26 on #1f2430 in ayu-mirage (and #1c1917 on dark). The description textarea itself measured correct (204,202,194 = --ink) in all four themes before the change; the black text appears in the title field while editing the item.\nFix: input.hov / textarea.hov hover and focus-visible keep color: var(--ink); textarea.desc-in/.md state color: var(--ink) explicitly.\nMeasured after (focused+hovered): title ayu-mirage rgb(204,202,194) on rgb(31,36,48) 9.5:1; light 14.6; dark 14.8; novita 13.2. Description textarea same values. Before: title ayu-mirage rgb(24,28,38) (about 1.1:1), dark rgb(28,25,23).\nSweep: no [data-theme=dark] or prefers-color-scheme selectors remain in CSS (only the :root theme blocks); the two JS matchMedia uses only pick the OS theme. Inputs reached by .hov: title-in and note-title (fixed). All other inputs/textareas/selects measured at least 8.9:1 in settings, board and item pages. Shots: tests/out/shots/wi227-after-*.png in the worktree.
